        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Products: 527 Euryanthe\n- People: Max Wolf, Carl Maria von Weber\n- Concepts: minor planets, nitrogen, opera, Romantic school\n\nFacts:\n- In 1904, Max Wolf discovered 527 Euryanthe orbiting the Sun.\n- 527 Euryanthe is a minor planet described as full of nitrogen.\n- 527 Euryanthe was named after the heroine of an opera by Carl Maria von Weber.\n- Carl Maria von Weber was a German composer, conductor, pianist, guitarist, and critic.\n- Carl Maria von Weber was one of the first significant composers of the Romantic school.",
